SYMBOL bv 160 256 R0
WINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 0
SYMATTR InstName Bmic
SYMATTR Value V=sin(2*pi*100*time)+0.3*sin(2*pi*430*time)
SYMBOL cap 280 200 R90
WINDOW 0 0 32 VBottom 2
WINDOW 3 32 32 VTop 2
SYMATTR InstName Cmic
SYMATTR Value 1u
SYMBOL res 304 240 R0
SYMATTR InstName Rbias
SYMATTR Value 33k
SYMBOL bv 560 256 R0
WINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 0
SYMATTR InstName Bprimary
SYMATTR Value V=absdelay(V(ambient),{Lead})
SYMBOL bv 880 256 R0
WINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 0
SYMATTR InstName Binvert
SYMATTR Value V=-{Gain}*V(mic)
SYMBOL bv 1200 256 R0
WINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 0
SYMATTR InstName Bsecondary
SYMATTR Value V=absdelay(V(inv),{AppDelay+EarDelay+Wait})
SYMBOL bv 1520 256 R0
WINDOW 3 0 0 Invisible 0
SYMATTR InstName Bear
SYMATTR Value V=V(noise)+V(anti)
TEXT 64 48 Left 3 ;PHONE ANC - TIMING AND PHASE IN LTSPICE
TEXT 64 120 Left 2 ;1   MICROPHONE INPUT
TEXT 464 120 Left 2 ;2   NOISE AT EAR
TEXT 784 120 Left 2 ;3   INVERTING GAIN
TEXT 1104 120 Left 2 ;4   PHONE + EARPHONE
TEXT 1424 120 Left 2 ;5   EAR PRESSURE
TEXT 64 160 Left 2 ;100 Hz + 430 Hz / RC high-pass
TEXT 464 160 Left 2 ;5 ms acoustic path
TEXT 784 160 Left 2 ;95% antinoise amplitude
TEXT 1104 160 Left 2 ;2 ms or 20 ms app delay
TEXT 80 488 Left 2 !.param Lead=5m EarDelay=1m Gain=0.95
TEXT 80 528 Left 2 !.param Wait=max(Lead-AppDelay-EarDelay,0)
TEXT 80 568 Left 2 !.step param AppDelay list 2m 20m
TEXT 80 608 Left 2 !.tran 0 100m 0 10u
TEXT 80 648 Left 2 !.meas tran NoiseRMS RMS V(noise) FROM 30m TO 100m
TEXT 80 688 Left 2 !.meas tran ResidualRMS RMS V(residual) FROM 30m TO 100m
TEXT 80 728 Left 2 !.meas tran Reduction_dB param 20*log10(NoiseRMS/ResidualRMS)
TEXT 80 800 Left 2 ;Voltage represents normalized sound pressure. Delay blocks model the paths; they are not phone hardware.
TEXT 80 840 Left 2 ;Run the schematic, then view V(noise), V(anti), V(residual). Right-click a B source to inspect its equation.
